    "notes": [
      "Native WebGPU/TSL flash-flood sample; all simulation, optics, effects and RTX integration are project-owned MJS.",
      "A deterministic shallow-water heightfield drives a travelling surge, standing waves, hydraulic foam, spray, mist and floating timber through a valley-scale gorge.",
      "Native RTX ray queries add static-gorge reflections, sunset-key visibility and ambient occlusion from live water depth/normal/roughness guides.",
      "A connected 2.8 by 2.5 kilometre textured upland grounds the gorge; two non-occluding 3D mountain ranges close the distant sunset horizon.",
      "Ten deterministic MJS-generated surface families provide 30 shared albedo, roughness and normal maps for terrain, rock, vegetation, timber, concrete, asphalt, metal and animated water flow.",
      "Water refraction, absorption and phase-locked caustics remain honest Three.js/TSL effects because the generic bridge exposes no refraction-ray API.",
      "No HUD, native/C++ source, downloaded model, image texture or external asset is required."
    ]
